            <ArticleTitle>Neurobrucellosis: an often forgotten cause of chronic meningitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0049475515592571</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 26-year-old man of neurobrucellosis who presented with intermittent fever and headache for 2 years, sensori-neural hearing loss with cerebellar ataxia. He responded well to a combination of antimicrobials with significant clinical improvement.</AbstractText>
